{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.JacobianOneDim","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.PiL2","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Comp","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.FundThmCalculus","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Measurable","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Pow","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.MeanValue"],"declarations":66,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_eq_zero_height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_eq_zero_height","kind":"theorem","line":756,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L756-L766","doc":"**Height-coordinate separation** (unconditional): `dH x y = 0` forces the\nheights to agree, `y₂ = x₂`.  The vertical half of the full separation axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_ge_logHeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_ge_logHeight","kind":"theorem","line":751,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L751-L754","doc":"**`dH` dominates the vertical log-drop** — `ofReal |log(y₂/x₂)| ≤ dH x y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH_ge_logHeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH_ge_logHeight","kind":"theorem","line":659,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L659-L748","doc":"**z-component length lower bound.**  Every admissible path from `x` to `y`\nhas hyperbolic length at least `|log (y₂/x₂)|` — the vertical drop is a lower\nbound for the hyperbolic length, via the FTC applied to `t ↦ log (γ(t)₂)`\n(finite length ⇒ the derivative is integrable, defeating the Cantor obstruction).\nUnconditional (no geodesic-uniqueness hypothesis). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.deriv_coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.deriv_coord","kind":"theorem","line":652,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L652-L657","doc":"Component derivative: `d/dt (γ t) i = (deriv γ t) i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.abs_coord_le_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.abs_coord_le_norm","kind":"theorem","line":641,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L641-L650","doc":"`|p i| ≤ ‖p‖` in Euclidean space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.coordCLM_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.coordCLM_apply","kind":"theorem","line":639,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L639-L639","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.coordCLM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.coordCLM","kind":"def","line":635,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L635-L637","doc":"Component `p ↦ p i` as a continuous linear functional on `E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_triangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_triangle","kind":"theorem","line":626,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L626-L633","doc":"**Triangle inequality** `dH x z ≤ dH x y + dH y z`.  DERIVED via the\nzero-speed reparametrised concatenation: the concatenation of an admissible\n`x → y` path and an admissible `y → z` path is admissible `x → z` and has\nhyperbolic length the sum of the two, so the infimum is subadditive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH_concat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH_concat","kind":"theorem","line":556,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L556-L623","doc":"**Length additivity of the concatenation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.deriv_concat_eq_R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.deriv_concat_eq_R","kind":"theorem","line":548,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L548-L554","doc":"`deriv (concat γ δ) = deriv (concatR δ)` on `(1/2, 1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.deriv_concat_eq_L","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.deriv_concat_eq_L","kind":"theorem","line":537,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L537-L546","doc":"`deriv (concat γ δ) = deriv (concatL γ)` on `[0, 1/2]` (both `0` at the join). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_rhoR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_rhoR","kind":"theorem","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L531-L535","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_rhoL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_rhoL","kind":"theorem","line":526,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L526-L529","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L485-L523","doc":"**The concatenation is admissible** from `x` to `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concat_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concat_half","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L468-L483","doc":"**The concatenation is differentiable at the join `1/2`** (both one-sided\nderivatives vanish). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat_eq_R_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat_eq_R_ge","kind":"theorem","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L456-L466","doc":"On `[1/2, ∞)` the concatenation agrees with the right branch, using the\njoin-matching `γ 1 = δ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat_eq_R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat_eq_R","kind":"theorem","line":453,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L453-L454","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat_eq_L","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat_eq_L","kind":"theorem","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L450-L451","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concatR_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concatR_half","kind":"theorem","line":439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L439-L447","doc":"The right branch has zero derivative at the join `s = 1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concatL_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concatL_half","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L429-L437","doc":"The left branch has zero derivative at the join `s = 1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concatR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concatR","kind":"theorem","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L419-L427","doc":"HasDerivAt for the right branch at points where `sprof (2s-1) ∈ [0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concatL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_concatL","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L410-L417","doc":"HasDerivAt for the left branch at points where `sprof (2s) ∈ [0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concatR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concatR","kind":"def","line":407,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L407-L408","doc":"Right branch as a standalone function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concatL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concatL","kind":"def","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L405-L406","doc":"Left branch as a standalone function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.concat","kind":"def","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L401-L403","doc":"The zero-speed reparametrised concatenation of `γ` and `δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.monotoneOn_of_hasDerivAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.monotoneOn_of_hasDerivAt","kind":"theorem","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L388-L398","doc":"`MonotoneOn` on `Icc a b` from a nonnegative pointwise derivative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.sprof_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.sprof_mem","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L377-L386","doc":"`sprof` maps `[0,1]` into `[0,1]`: `sprof w = w²(3−2w) ≥ 0` and\n`1 − sprof w = (1−w)²(1+2w) ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH_reparam_segment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH_reparam_segment","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L339-L375","doc":"**Reparametrisation length invariance (segment form).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.sprof_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.sprof_one","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L337-L337","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.sprof_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.sprof_zero","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L336-L336","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_sprof","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.hasDerivAt_sprof","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L328-L335","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.sprof","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.sprof","kind":"def","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L326-L327","doc":"Smooth monotone reparametrisation profile `s(t) = 3t² − 2t³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.dH_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.dH_eq","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L316-L322","doc":"**`dH` is invariant under an involutive conformal height-scaling map.**  Both\nboundary isometries are involutions, so this is the form they use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.dH_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.dH_le","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L308-L314","doc":"**`dH (φ x) (φ y) ≤ dH x y`** — for each admissible `γ`, `φ∘γ` is admissible\nwith equal length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.pathLenH_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.pathLenH_comp","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L298-L306","doc":"`φ` preserves hyperbolic path length: `len (φ∘γ) = len γ` — the integral of\nthe pointwise-preserved speed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.admissiblePath_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.admissiblePath_comp","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L288-L296","doc":"The image of an admissible path under `φ` is admissible (endpoints move by\n`φ`, `H³` is preserved, differentiability is by the chain rule). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.speed_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.speed_comp","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L269-L286","doc":"**The pointwise line-element preservation** — the mathematical heart.  At any\npoint of `H³`, the hyperbolic *speed* `‖γ'‖/z` of `φ ∘ γ` equals that of `γ`: the\nconformal factor `lam` multiplies both `‖γ'‖` (via the chain rule + `hconf`) and\n`z` (via `hheight`), and cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.maps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.maps","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L264-L267","doc":"A conformal height-scaling map sends `H³` into `H³` (the height stays\npositive: `lam·z > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.hheight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.hheight","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.hconf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.hconf","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L256-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.hlam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.hlam","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L255-L255","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.hderiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.hderiv","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L254-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.lam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.lam","kind":"def","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L253-L253","doc":"the conformal factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.Dφ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.Dφ","kind":"def","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L251-L251","doc":"the Fréchet derivative field of `φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry.mk","kind":"ctor","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L249-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.IsDHIsometry","kind":"structure","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L244-L257","doc":"**Conformal height-scaling data for `φ`.**  A choice of derivative field `Dφ`\nand conformal factor `lam` witnessing that `φ` is, on `H³`, differentiable with a\nderivative that scales every tangent norm by `lam(p)` and scales the height\ncoordinate by the SAME `lam(p)`.  Carries data (`Dφ`, `lam`), so it is a\n`structure`, not a `Prop`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_comm","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L229-L232","doc":"**`dH` is symmetric** — `dH x y = dH y x`.  DERIVED (bean `qou-322e`, symmetry\nleg), not adopted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_comm_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_comm_le","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L222-L227","doc":"**`dH x y ≤ dH y x`** — each admissible `δ : y → x` reverses to an admissible\n`x → y` path of equal length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L209-L220","doc":"**Reverse path length preservation** — the reversed path has the same\nhyperbolic length as the original.  The integrand at `t` is the original's\nintegrand at `1 − t` (`norm_deriv_reverse` for the numerator; the height is\n`γ(1−t)_z` on both sides), and the reflection change of variables closes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.norm_deriv_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.norm_deriv_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L197-L207","doc":"The reversed path's speed matches the original at the reflected point:\n`‖(γ∘(1−·))'(t)‖ = ‖γ'(1−t)‖` (the chain-rule factor `−1` has norm `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.reverse_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.reverse_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L184-L195","doc":"The reverse path `t ↦ γ(1−t)` of an admissible `γ : x → y` is admissible from\n`y` to `x` (endpoints swap; `H³` and differentiability are preserved because\n`1 − t ∈ [0,1]` whenever `t ∈ [0,1]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.reflect_lintegral_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.reflect_lintegral_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L164-L182","doc":"**Reflection change of variables on `[0,1]`** — `∫⁻_{[0,1]} u = ∫⁻_{[0,1]}\nu(1−·)`, from Mathlib's antitone one-dimensional Jacobian formula applied to the\nreflection `t ↦ 1 − t` (whose derivative is `−1`, `|−1| = 1`, and which maps\n`[0,1]` onto itself).  Holds for ANY `u`, no measurability required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_self","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L142-L153","doc":"**`dH x x = 0`** for `x ∈ H³`: the constant path at `x` is admissible and has\nhyperbolic length `0` (its derivative vanishes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L139-L140","doc":"The distance is nonnegative — automatic in `ℝ≥0∞`, recorded for readers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_le_pathLenH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_le_pathLenH","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L134-L137","doc":"Any admissible path bounds the distance from above: `dH x y ≤ len γ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L128-L132","doc":"**The hyperbolic distance** `dH x y`: the infimum of hyperbolic lengths over\nadmissible paths from `x` to `y`.  A DERIVED object — an infimum of the line\nelement — not an adopted metric tensor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.diff","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.mem","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.target","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.source","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath.mk","kind":"ctor","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L122-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.AdmissiblePath","kind":"structure","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L118-L126","doc":"**An admissible path** from `x` to `y`: a path landing in `H³` on `[0,1]`,\ndifferentiable there, with the right endpoints.  Differentiability on `[0,1]`\n(not merely continuity) is what makes `pathLenH` measure the honest length — a\ncontinuous-only class admits length-`0` Cantor paths between distinct points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.pathLenH","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L111-L116","doc":"**Hyperbolic path length** `∫ ‖γ'(t)‖ / γ(t)_z dt` over `[a,b]`: the\nRiemannian line element `ds = ‖dx‖ / z` of `ds² = (dx²+dy²+dz²)/z²` integrated\nalong `γ`.  Written with the real ratio inside `ENNReal.ofReal` so that the\nconformal cancellation of the isometry engine is an elementary real identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.mem_upperH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.mem_upperH","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.upperH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.upperH","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L105-L107","doc":"**Upper half-space** `H³ = {(x,y,z) : z > 0}`, the same predicate as\n`HyperbolicVolume.upperHalfSpace` on the Euclidean carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.E","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetric.lean#L100-L103","doc":"The carrier of the upper half-space model: `ℝ³` with its Euclidean inner\nproduct (needed for tangent-vector norms and the inversion's conformal\nderivative). ","signatureChunk":0}]}